% Generate pdd/server/routes/auth.py for local-browser credential discovery.

Export an APIRouter with prefix /api/v1/auth and tag auth.
Use Pydantic response models and CloudConfig's explicit self-hosted configuration.
GET /status returns authenticated, cached=false, and expires_at=null.
POST /login returns success when configuration exists; otherwise explain the URL and token variables.
GET /login/poll/{poll_id} returns status=error explaining configured bearer authentication.
POST /logout returns success=false and instructions to unset credentials, restart connect, and revoke server tokens.
GET /jwt-token retains the compatibility response {jwt: token|null}.
Before returning credentials, require a loopback request client.
If Origin exists, require localhost or a loopback IP, including IPv6.
Reject remote clients or external origins with HTTP 403.
POST /test checks listSessions using the configured bearer token and a 10-second timeout.
Return success/message/status_code, or a connection failure without exposing credentials.
Do not initiate OAuth, open a browser, read keyrings, or mutate identity caches.
